{"id":"twitter:1892985021708861687","tweet_id":"1892985021708861687","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1892985021708861687","title":"@WhittiGuySky @SiljaLynx @elonmusk One thing we teach students when using LLMs is to find the authors and source the model is using. One way to establ","summary":"@WhittiGuySky @SiljaLynx @elonmusk One thing we teach students when using LLMs is to find the authors and source the model is using. One way to establish the credibility of those claims is to see if you can triangulate the answer with other data Sure does look to me in terms of volume, Elion = 1. https://t.co/plcnuZ5UlJ","date":"2025-02-21","published":"2025-02-21T17:09:33+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/ExaminaOmnia/status/1892984257288556870","reply_tweet_id":"1892984257288556870","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@WhittiGuySky @SiljaLynx @elonmusk One thing we teach students when using LLMs is to find the authors and source the model is using.<br><br>One way to establish the credibility of those claims is to see if you can triangulate the answer with other data<br><br>Sure does look to me in terms of volume, Elion = 1. <a href=\"https://t.co/plcnuZ5UlJ\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/plcnuZ5UlJ</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/5257b17c3c8f963f7c522e8933ff7c46.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/b23540c13e99686706df9c803247ea5b.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1892985021708861687","display_date":"February 21, 2025 · 17:09 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/5257b17c3c8f963f7c522e8933ff7c46.jpg","/archive/twitter/media/b23540c13e99686706df9c803247ea5b.jpg"]}
