{"id":"twitter:1892363567115989082","tweet_id":"1892363567115989082","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1892363567115989082","title":"@mira_2heal @RealisticPoetry I realized I made one mistake. Japanese is a syllabic language. Not logographic Chinese is logographic. Each symbol is a ","summary":"@mira_2heal @RealisticPoetry I realized I made one mistake. Japanese is a syllabic language. Not logographic Chinese is logographic. Each symbol is a word. There are 1,000s of symbols. In Japanese each symbol is a syllable. 100s of symbols. English is phonetic. 44 sounds and 26 syllables","date":"2025-02-20","published":"2025-02-20T00:00:07+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/mira_2heal/status/1888847780350918776","reply_tweet_id":"1888847780350918776","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@mira_2heal @RealisticPoetry I realized I made one mistake.<br><br>Japanese is a syllabic language. Not logographic<br><br>Chinese is logographic. Each symbol is a word. There are 1,000s of symbols.<br><br>In Japanese each symbol is a syllable. 100s of symbols.<br><br>English is phonetic. 44 sounds and 26 syllables</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1892363567115989082","display_date":"February 20, 2025 · 00:00 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
