{"id":"twitter:2048808848333455810","tweet_id":"2048808848333455810","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2048808848333455810","title":"Bahrianyi escaped the prison camp, he would escape russian and German capture throughout his life \"It's better to die running than to live rotting,\" h","summary":"Bahrianyi escaped the prison camp, he would escape russian and German capture throughout his life \"It's better to die running than to live rotting,\" he would write in the novel Tiger Trappers, which was semi-autobiographical https://t.co/vxCMDy3SZj","date":"2026-04-27","published":"2026-04-27T16:57:49+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2048804712242094217","reply_tweet_id":"2048804712242094217","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Bahrianyi escaped the prison camp, he would escape russian and German capture throughout his life<br><br>&quot;It&#x27;s better to die running than to live rotting,&quot; he would write in the novel Tiger Trappers, which was semi-autobiographical <a href=\"https://t.co/vxCMDy3SZj\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/vxCMDy3SZj</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/577ea224c323cc9e6eb1a9f4463ecc8f.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2048808848333455810","display_date":"April 27, 2026 · 16:57 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/577ea224c323cc9e6eb1a9f4463ecc8f.jpg"]}
{"id":"twitter:2048804712242094217","tweet_id":"2048804712242094217","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2048804712242094217","title":"On April 16, 1932, 25-year-old Ivan Bahrianyi was arrested after his poetry was labeled subversive He spent 11 months in solitary confinement and afte","summary":"On April 16, 1932, 25-year-old Ivan Bahrianyi was arrested after his poetry was labeled subversive He spent 11 months in solitary confinement and after three years was \"released\" to Siberian exile. https://t.co/UVVVODcwa6","date":"2026-04-27","published":"2026-04-27T16:41:23+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2048802836268437626","reply_tweet_id":"2048802836268437626","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>On April 16, 1932, 25-year-old Ivan Bahrianyi was arrested after his poetry was labeled subversive<br><br>He spent 11 months in solitary confinement and after three years was &quot;released&quot; to Siberian exile. <a href=\"https://t.co/UVVVODcwa6\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/UVVVODcwa6</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/57e29f5263d5d8d840dd031bcfb5663e.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2048804712242094217","display_date":"April 27, 2026 · 16:41 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/57e29f5263d5d8d840dd031bcfb5663e.jpg"]}
