{"id":"twitter:1890077264244797745","tweet_id":"1890077264244797745","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1890077264244797745","title":"If people are talking to you about DOGE and possible unauthorized access. Ask them if they know -FISMA -FIPS 199/200 -OMB-130 If they don't know, don'","summary":"If people are talking to you about DOGE and possible unauthorized access. Ask them if they know -FISMA -FIPS 199/200 -OMB-130 If they don't know, don't talk to them about unauthorized access by DOGE (Bonus points if they know FedRAMP vs OTA and CFR 32 vs CFR 48)","date":"2025-02-13","published":"2025-02-13T16:35:10+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>If people are talking to you about DOGE and possible unauthorized access.<br><br>Ask them if they know<br>-FISMA<br>-FIPS 199/200<br>-OMB-130<br><br>If they don&#x27;t know, don&#x27;t talk to them about unauthorized access by DOGE<br><br>(Bonus points if they know FedRAMP vs OTA and CFR 32 vs CFR 48)</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1890077264244797745","display_date":"February 13, 2025 · 16:35 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1890075133613863112","tweet_id":"1890075133613863112","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1890075133613863112","title":"@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops The use of the CDN to process and store user data from a form however, may bring the CDN in scope. If that data gets","summary":"@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops The use of the CDN to process and store user data from a form however, may bring the CDN in scope. If that data gets stored or processed server side, and leaves government boundaries than that is not just a CDN serving up images from imagedelivery dot net It needs equivalency","date":"2025-02-13","published":"2025-02-13T16:26:42+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1890073904489902334","reply_tweet_id":"1890073904489902334","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops The use of the CDN to process and store user data from a form however, may bring the CDN in scope.<br><br>If that data gets stored or processed server side, and leaves government boundaries than that is not just a CDN serving up images from imagedelivery dot net<br><br>It needs equivalency</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1890075133613863112","display_date":"February 13, 2025 · 16:26 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1890073904489902334","tweet_id":"1890073904489902334","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1890073904489902334","title":"@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops There is a proposed rule in FAR to update the OTA process: https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/10/03/2023","summary":"@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops There is a proposed rule in FAR to update the OTA process: https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/10/03/2023-21327/federal-acquisition-regulation-standardizing-cybersecurity-requirements-for-unclassified-federal The key thing to remember while it is a waiver for FedRAMP it does not absolve you of other legal requirem","date":"2025-02-13","published":"2025-02-13T16:21:49+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1890073422656598410","reply_tweet_id":"1890073422656598410","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops There is a proposed rule in FAR to update the OTA process:<br><br><a href=\"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/10/03/2023-21327/federal-acquisition-regulation-standardizing-cybersecurity-requirements-for-unclassified-federal\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2023/10/03/2023-21327/federal-acquisition-regulation-standardizing-cybersecurity-requirements-for-unclassified-federal</a><br><br>The key thing to remember while it is a waiver for FedRAMP it does not absolve you of other legal requirements<br><br>(using a CDN for a Fedramp-low project like a website isn&#x27;t one)</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1890073904489902334","display_date":"February 13, 2025 · 16:21 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1890073422656598410","tweet_id":"1890073422656598410","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1890073422656598410","title":"@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops They are describing an OTA, which some contractors erroneously think skips FedRAMP, because sometimes it does when r","summary":"@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops They are describing an OTA, which some contractors erroneously think skips FedRAMP, because sometimes it does when rules aren't enforced OTA can't exceed 500m OTA have small business cut out 11 Agencies are authorized for OTA","date":"2025-02-13","published":"2025-02-13T16:19:54+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/rubicon49bc/status/1889764241676050590","reply_tweet_id":"1889764241676050590","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@rubicon49bc @beskardev @cyb3rops They are describing an OTA, which some contractors erroneously think skips FedRAMP, because sometimes it does when rules aren&#x27;t enforced<br><br>OTA can&#x27;t exceed 500m<br>OTA have small business cut out<br>11 Agencies are authorized for OTA</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1890073422656598410","display_date":"February 13, 2025 · 16:19 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
