{"id":"twitter:1885319515900158380","tweet_id":"1885319515900158380","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1885319515900158380","title":"@WildCardQ @ChrisMurphyCT Yes we do. There are very specific rules set out by Commerce and OMB on the handling of assets not meant for public release ","summary":"@WildCardQ @ChrisMurphyCT Yes we do. There are very specific rules set out by Commerce and OMB on the handling of assets not meant for public release when you have authorized access to Government systems. You can check them out in NIST-SP-800-53 and NIST-SP-800-53a But start with FIPS 199/200","date":"2025-01-31","published":"2025-01-31T13:29:34+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/WildCardQ/status/1885318353431953690","reply_tweet_id":"1885318353431953690","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@WildCardQ @ChrisMurphyCT Yes we do.<br><br>There are very specific rules set out by Commerce and OMB on the handling of assets not meant for public release when you have authorized access to Government systems.<br><br>You can check them out in NIST-SP-800-53 and NIST-SP-800-53a<br><br>But start with FIPS 199/200</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1885319515900158380","display_date":"January 31, 2025 · 13:29 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
