{"id":"twitter:1885001020499255562","tweet_id":"1885001020499255562","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1885001020499255562","title":"@alicenotmiller We were just covering the differences between Grimm's Fairy Tale spread and Pushkin's russian collections as a tool of statehood in my","summary":"@alicenotmiller We were just covering the differences between Grimm's Fairy Tale spread and Pushkin's russian collections as a tool of statehood in my children's literature class. Here in the states Russian Literature always been pitched as \"cool\" something for folks that are into \"jazz\" read","date":"2025-01-30","published":"2025-01-30T16:23:59+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1885000372764442864","reply_tweet_id":"1885000372764442864","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@alicenotmiller We were just covering the differences between Grimm&#x27;s Fairy Tale spread and Pushkin&#x27;s russian collections as a tool of statehood in my children&#x27;s literature class.<br><br>Here in the states Russian Literature always been pitched as &quot;cool&quot; something for folks that are into &quot;jazz&quot; read</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1885001020499255562","display_date":"January 30, 2025 · 16:23 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1885000372764442864","tweet_id":"1885000372764442864","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1885000372764442864","title":"@alicenotmiller I made the reference to Pushkin, because it is a very old thing. Russian Literature has always been pushed as \"High Art\" and even on t","summary":"@alicenotmiller I made the reference to Pushkin, because it is a very old thing. Russian Literature has always been pushed as \"High Art\" and even on the subversive side. You see a lot of brutalism and Samizdat aesthetic in old punk rock for example The cool nerds read samizdat chap books","date":"2025-01-30","published":"2025-01-30T16:21:25+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/alicenotmiller/status/1884999579122204795","reply_tweet_id":"1884999579122204795","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@alicenotmiller I made the reference to Pushkin, because it is a very old thing.<br><br>Russian Literature has always been pushed as &quot;High Art&quot;<br><br>and even on the subversive side. You see a lot of brutalism and Samizdat aesthetic in old punk rock for example<br><br>The cool nerds read samizdat chap books</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1885000372764442864","display_date":"January 30, 2025 · 16:21 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1884999353817034935","tweet_id":"1884999353817034935","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1884999353817034935","title":"@UK_Daniel_Card Not with prose like that. You must take advantage of White Space to succeed as an expert on LinkedIn I once stepped over a homeless ma","summary":"@UK_Daniel_Card Not with prose like that. You must take advantage of White Space to succeed as an expert on LinkedIn I once stepped over a homeless man, entering a store, but as he left he told me about the line break. From that day I learned to space out on nuclear pontifications.","date":"2025-01-30","published":"2025-01-30T16:17:22+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/UK_Daniel_Card/status/1884971143712416047","reply_tweet_id":"1884971143712416047","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@UK_Daniel_Card Not with prose like that.<br><br>You must take advantage of White Space to succeed as an expert on LinkedIn<br><br>I once stepped over a homeless man, entering a store, but as he left he told me about the line break.<br><br>From that day I learned to space out on nuclear pontifications.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1884999353817034935","display_date":"January 30, 2025 · 16:17 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1884998516130398311","tweet_id":"1884998516130398311","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1884998516130398311","title":"@johns2801 @HarrisonBecker7 We can model turn out and effects pretty well. Palast just did his every election cycle review on voter suprresion. The mo","summary":"@johns2801 @HarrisonBecker7 We can model turn out and effects pretty well. Palast just did his every election cycle review on voter suprresion. The most effective techniques aren't illegal. And the GOP has been doing them for decades. The fault lies in not recognizing the threat earlier. I missed it","date":"2025-01-30","published":"2025-01-30T16:14:02+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/johns2801/status/1884997298117100017","reply_tweet_id":"1884997298117100017","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@johns2801 @HarrisonBecker7 We can model  turn out and effects pretty well.<br><br>Palast just did his every election cycle review on voter suprresion.<br><br>The most effective techniques aren&#x27;t illegal.<br><br>And the GOP has been doing them for decades. The fault lies in not recognizing the threat earlier.<br><br>I missed it</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1884998516130398311","display_date":"January 30, 2025 · 16:14 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
